TEST: wifi: ath11k: experiment on the extension descriptor completion fault

Three switches for the bench, each with its own module parameter:

ext_slot_wide gives the extension descriptor slots the vendor's 136 byte
stride and clears the whole slot, the bytes past the descriptor too, each
time one is built. The TCL data length stays that of the descriptor. It is
read when the rings are allocated, so it takes effect with the next load of
the module.

tx_id_gen puts a generation in the two spare bits of the buffer id in the
TCL cookie, counted up each time the id is issued. A completion that returns
another generation is counted in tx_stale_compl and dropped without
releasing the frame the id holds now. The generation is always sent; the
switch decides whether it is checked, and can be changed at run time.

tx_compl_log keeps the last completion of each id, and prints it next to the
current one when a completion is stale, for an id that holds no frame, or
returns another address than the one queued for the id, which is counted in
tx_addr_mismatch.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
